   "summary": "READ: SC asks gov’t to comment on petition vs deferment of barangay, SK polls The poll body debunked on Facebook a post by Gallaza Sharly Paradise claiming that the elections would be held that month and the filing of certificates of candidacy (COCs) would begin on Oct. As a result, the next BSKE was moved to November 2028.",
   "summary_zh": "阅读：最高法院要求政府就推迟 barangay 和 SK 选举的请愿发表意见。选举管理机构在 Facebook 上否认了 Gallaza Sharly Paradise 发布的帖子，该帖声称选举将于当月举行，候选人资格证书（COCs）的提交也将于10月开始。因此，下一次基层和青年理事会选举（BSKE）已推迟至2028年11月。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "READ: SC asks gov’t to comment on petition vs deferment of barangay, SK polls The poll body debunked on Facebook a post by Gallaza Sharly Paradise claiming that the elections would be held that month and the filing of certificates of candidacy (COCs) would begin on Oct. 26. “There will be no Barangay and Sangguniang Kabataan (SK) elections this year under the current law, and the filing of [COCs] scheduled for Oct. 26, 2026, will not take place,” the Comelec said. President Marcos signed Republic Act No. 12326 into law on Sept. 24, extending the terms of barangay and youth officials from three years to five years. As a result, the next BSKE was moved to November 2028. —Chelsy Claire Perez",
