   "title": "Man on run for 25 years held in bihar fodder case 101792781098855",
   "url": "https://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/man-on-run-for-25-years-held-in-bihar-fodder-case-101792781098855.html",
   "domain": "hindustantimes.com",
   "source": "hindustantimes.com",
   "published": "Sat, 24 Oct 2026 07:44:30 +0530",
   "_dt": 1792808070.0,
   "ageDays": 0.04,
   "summary": "The Central Bureau of Investigation (CBI) has arrested a proclaimed offender, Satyendra Kumar, who was wanted in Bihar’s fodder scam cases and remained elusive for over 25 years. Rashtriya Janata Dal (RJD) chief Lalu Prasad Yadav has been convicted in five fodder scam cases relating to fraudulent withdrawals from the Chaibasa, Deoghar, Dumka and Doranda treasuries during his tenure as Bihar chief minister.",
   "summary_zh": "印度中央调查局（CBI）已逮捕一名公开宣布脱离隐匿状态的罪犯Satyendra Kumar；此人因涉及比哈尔邦饲料诈骗案而一直遭到通缉，并在逃超过25年。Rashtriya Janata Dal（RJD）党首Lalu Prasad Yadav在5起饲料诈骗案中被判有罪，这些案件涉及他在担任比哈尔邦首席部长期间对Chaibasa、Deoghar、Dumka和Doranda国库进行的欺诈性提取。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The Central Bureau of Investigation (CBI) has arrested a proclaimed offender, Satyendra Kumar, who was wanted in Bihar’s fodder scam cases and remained elusive for over 25 years. Kumar, an agency spokesperson said in a statement, was named by CBI in one of the fodder scam charge sheets in 2001. “After filing of the charge sheet, Kumar absconded and CBI was on his look out for over 25 years,” the spokesperson said. “As he failed to appear before the court to face trial, a permanent warrant of arrest was issued against him by the court,” the spokesperson added. The agency said that serious efforts were made to trace him. “Based on sustained physical and technical surveillance, coupled with human intelligence, Kumar’s location was traced to Nepal. Recently, he entered India and was travelling from Guna (Madhya Pradesh) to Lucknow by train on Thursday. A dedicated CBI team was formed to arrest Kumar on his way from Guna to Lucknow. The team was deployed at Lucknow railway station before the train’s arrival. Around midnight, he was apprehended,” the spokesperson said. The agency said that Kumar was being brought to Ranchi on transit remand. It, however, didn’t elaborate his role in the fodder scam cases. Rashtriya Janata Dal (RJD) chief Lalu Prasad Yadav has been convicted in five fodder scam cases relating to fraudulent withdrawals from the Chaibasa, Deoghar, Dumka and Doranda treasuries during his tenure as Bihar chief minister. The multi-crore fodder scam comprises 55 cases involving alleged fraudulent withdrawals of around ₹ 950 crore from the undivided Bihar treasury between 1992 and 1995 through fake bills for fodder, medicines and equipment. In July this year, the Supreme Court declined to cancel the bail granted to Yadav in 2021",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
