   "summary_zh": "阿布贾，Deji Elumoye与Juliet Akoje。总统夫人、参议员Oluremi Tinubu宣布，尼日利亚正走在实现全面经济复苏和可持续发展的正确道路上，并强调投资者对尼日利亚经济的信心已大幅提升。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Deji Elumoye and Juliet Akoje in Abuja Wife of the President, Senator Oluremi Tinubu, has declared that Nigeria is on the right path to total economic recovery and sustainable development emphasising that the confidence of investors in the nation’s economy has greatly improved. Speaking yesterday while inaugurating the PBAT Door-to-Door Movement Headquarters in Abuja, the First Lady stressed that the country’s economic recovery is looking up with both local and international investors having hope in Nigeria’s economy. She urged members of the Movement to not just go door-to-door but pass on the message of hope assured and shared prosperity. “As we embark on this noble mission, let us always remember that impactful outreach extends far beyond visiting doorsteps. Our message must consistently resonate hope, peace, unity and development, especially the impactful progress the Tinubu administration has made so far.” Mrs. Tinubu commended the leadership and members of the Movement for already traversing 14 states of the federation urging them to sustain the momentum as the APC presidential campaign formally kicks off. In his remarks, Senate President, Senator Godswill Akpabio stated that the message to Nigerians is to have faith in the steady but assured improvement in the nation generally. “The message is that hope is here, hope has come and hope is alive.” Also speaking, Delta State Governor, Hon. Sheriff Oborevwori, was unequivocal in his declaration that the sub-nationals are having it much better under President Tinubu saying state revenues have improved in such a way that workers are not being owed salaries and contractors are being paid promptly. Convener of the PBAT Door-to-Door Movement, High Chief Government Ekpemupolo, in a speech read on his behalf by High Chief Matthew Tonlagha, assured that the movement will take the message to every nook and cranny of the nation to ensure victory for President Tinubu come January 2027. Also yesterday, the First Lady performed the Foundation laying ceremony of a state-of-the -art Renewed Hope Startup Hub in Wuye, Abuja. The hub is partnership between the National Information Technology Development Agency (NITDA) and the Government of Japan through its Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA). Mrs. Tinubu described the hub as yet another important step towards technological advancement, youth empowerment and digital inclusion for youth across the nation. According to her, “The establishment of start-up hubs across the nation aligns with the Renewed Hope Agenda of President Bola Tinubu, which prioritises youth empowerment through entrepreneurship, skills development and sustainable job creation, equipping young Nigerians to compete and thrive in the global economy. “To our young innovators, this start-up hub is yours. You can arrive here with a sketch and leave with a working prototype that takes you into the global market space. Let this hub be the home where your dreams are nurtured and scaled.” She commended the collaboration between the government of Japan and Nigeria which she noted with admiration that it birthed the startup hub and many other developmental projects and initiatives. In his remarks, DG/CEO of NITDA, Mallam Kashifu Inuwa Abdullahi, noted that since 2021 the partnership between the organisation and JICA focused on strengthening Nigeria’s innovation and entrepreneurship ecosystem through capacity building, knowledge transfer, infrastructure development and international collaboration. He said the proposed facility is intended to serve as a focal point for startup development, industry engagement and innovation ecosystem coordination that will strengthen access to infrastructure, technical expertise, mentorship and opportunities for collaboration between Nigerian innovators and international partners. “This partnership is an investment of approximately US$10.4 million depending on the conversion rate for the innovation hub. The project is also presented as part of a broader Japan–Nigeria start-up ecosystem support initiative involving complementary financing mechanisms.” On his part, Japanese Ambassador to Nigeria, Suzuki Hideo, promised that with the improved economic atmosphere in the country, Japan is pleased to continue to expand its partnerships with Nigeria especially in the areas of education and technology. Founded on January 22, 1995, THISDAY is published by THISDAY NEWSPAPERS LTD., 35 Creek Road Apapa, Lagos, Nigeria with offices in 36 states of Nigeria , the Federal Capital Territory and around the world. It is Nigeria’s most authoritative news media available on all platforms for the political, business, professional and diplomatic elite and broader middle classes while serving as the meeting point of new ideas, culture and technology for the aspirationals and millennials. The newspaper is a public trust dedicated to the pursuit of truth and reason covering a range of issues from breaking news to politics, business, the markets, the arts, sports and community to the crossroads of people and society. You can email us at: hello@thisdaylive.com or visit our contact us page",
