   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription Bharat Petroleum’s standalone net profits in the September-end quarter fell 22.5% on a year-over-year basis as volatile crude prices impacted margins following the reignited conflict in West Asia. The Mumbai-headquartered refiner’s net profit declined to ₹4,993.17 crore in the reported quarter compared to ₹6,442.5 crore in the same period last year.",
   "summary_zh": "巴拉特石油公司截至9月底季度的独立净利润同比下降22.5%，原因是西亚冲突重新爆发后，原油价格波动影响了利润率。这家总部位于孟买的炼油商当季净利润降至4993.17亿卢比，而去年同期为6442.5亿卢比。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Bharat Petroleum’s standalone net profits in the September-end quarter fell 22.5% on a year-over-year basis as volatile crude prices impacted margins following the reignited conflict in West Asia. The Mumbai-headquartered refiner’s net profit declined to ₹4,993.17 crore in the reported quarter compared to ₹6,442.5 crore in the same period last year. The state-owned oil-marketing company’s cost of materials consumed soared 44.2% during the period to ₹74,969 crore. Revenues increased about 30% on a year-over-year basis to more than ₹1.58 lakh crore. The refiners’ physical performance reported an uptick. It rose 6% during the mentioned period to 10.41 million metric tonnes (MMT). Also read | Strike by lorry drivers at BPCL depot in Salem withdrawn Its peer Hindustan Petroleum had reported a 9% decline in standalone net profits on Thursday. Delhi-headquartered peer Indian Oil is scheduled to post their September-end financial results on October 30. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
