   "title": "Judge orders Trump to give deposition in BBC lawsuit by December 11",
   "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/judge-orders-trump-to-give-deposition-in-bbc-lawsuit-by-december-11/article71613501.ece",
   "domain": "thehindu.com",
   "source": "thehindu.com",
   "published": "Fri, 23 Oct 2026 07:22:38 +0530",
   "_dt": 1792720358.0,
   "ageDays": 1.05,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription A U.S. judge on Thursday (October 22, 2026) issued President Donald Trump a December 11 deadline to testify under oath in his $10 billion defamation lawsuit against the BBC . Judge Enjolique Lett in Miami gave the order in response to complaints by the British broadcaster that Mr. Trump has refused to sit for a deposition, including canceling a previously agreed date of October 16.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅A即可解锁这些内容。美国法官于2026年10月22日星期四向唐纳德·特朗普总统下达最后期限，要求其在针对BBC的100亿美元诽谤诉讼中宣誓作证。迈阿密法官恩乔利克·莱特针对英国广播公司的投诉作出该命令；该 broadcaster 称，特朗普先生拒绝接受宣誓取证，包括取消此前商定的10月16日取证日期。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription A U.S. judge on Thursday (October 22, 2026) issued President Donald Trump a December 11 deadline to testify under oath in his $10 billion defamation lawsuit against the BBC . Judge Enjolique Lett in Miami gave the order in response to complaints by the British broadcaster that Mr. Trump has refused to sit for a deposition, including canceling a previously agreed date of October 16. If Mr. Trump fails to attend the deposition by then, he risks sanctions, including dismissal of his lawsuit, the court said. Mr. Trump has accused the BBC of deceptively editing its documentary \"Trump: A Second Chance\" to make it seem as if he was inciting violence when he told supporters to march on the U.S. Capitol on January 6, 2021, after losing the presidential election. The crowd proceeded to storm Congress in an attempt to stop the formal certification of Democrat Joe Biden's victory. While the BBC has apologised for the incident, which prompted the resignation of multiple senior executives, the broadcaster has denied it caused Mr. Trump any real injury and moved for the case to be dismissed. Mr. Trump filed his suit against the BBC in December 2025 and is seeking at least $5 billion on each of two counts. Charles Tobin, a lawyer for the BBC , said in court that Mr. Trump had no real excuse not to testify and that on October 16, he had only been campaigning, \"participating in party politics.\" In a court filing Wednesday (October 21), Mr. Trump's legal team argued that he was not seeking to avoid a deposition but had been constrained by \"matters of national importance.\" The lawyers said Mr. Trump would be able to give a deposition between January 11 and 22. Mr. Trump has made attacks on the media a signature of his two presidential terms, insulting reporters who ask questions he doesn't like and seeking to ban outlets airing critical reports from the White House. Most recently, the administration has plunged into a legal dispute with CNN, MSNOW and Politico over attempts to bar them from the White House. With his approval ratings in the low 30% range and polls showing his Republican Party likely to lose control of the House of Representatives in the November 3 midterm elections, Mr. Trump faces increasing headwinds as he approaches his final years in power. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "af"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol",
    "sec"
   ],
   "tier": 2,
   "actor": "美国",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
   "usHit": true,
   "terrHit": false,
   "riskHit": false,
   "riskKind": "",
   "score": 0.6,
   "tag": "rss_thehindu",
   "title_zh": "法官命令特朗普于12月11日前就BBC诉讼案宣誓作证",
   "body_zh": "订阅可享受独家报道、社论、观点等更多内容。购买订阅即可解锁这些权益。美国法官于周四（2026年10月22日）向唐纳德·特朗普总统下达最后期限，要求他在针对英国广播公司BBC的100亿美元诽谤诉讼中于12月11日前宣誓作证。迈阿密法官恩朱利克·莱特针对英国广播公司的投诉作出这项命令。该广播公司称，特朗普先生拒绝接受庭外取证，包括取消此前约定的10月16日作证日期。法院表示，如果特朗普先生届时未能出席庭外取证，他可能面临制裁，包括诉讼被驳回。特朗普先生指控BBC欺骗性地剪辑其纪录片《特朗普：第二次机会》，使他2021年1月6日在大选失利后呼吁支持者进军美国国会大厦时，看起来像是在煽动暴力。随后，人群冲向国会，试图阻止对民主党人乔·拜登胜选的正式确认。尽管BBC已就这一事件道歉，该事件还导致多名高级管理人员辞职，但广播公司否认自己给特朗普先生造成了任何实际伤害，并请求法院驳回此案。特朗普先生于2025年12月对BBC提起诉讼，要求就两项指控分别获得至少50亿美元赔偿。BBC的律师查尔斯·托宾在庭上表示，特朗普先生没有真正的理由拒绝作证；10月16日，他只是在“参与政党政治”并开展竞选活动。特朗普先生的律师团队周三（10月21日）提交法院文件称，他并非想逃避庭外取证，而是受到“具有全国重要性的事务”的限制。律师们表示，特朗普先生能够在1月11日至22日之间接受庭外取证。特朗普先生把攻击媒体作为其两届总统任期的标志性做法，侮辱提出他不喜欢的问题的记者，并试图禁止报道批评性内容的媒体进入白宫。最近，美国政府与CNN、MSNOW和Politico陷入法律争端，原因在于政府试图禁止这些媒体进入白宫。随着特朗普先生的支持率降至30%出头，调查显示共和党可能在11月3日的中期选举中失去对众议院的控制；在距离其执政最后几年之际，他面临越来越多的阻力。评论必须使用英文，并以完整句子表述。评论不得含有辱骂性内容或针对个人。请遵守我们的社区评论准则。我们已迁移至新的评论平台。如果你已是《The Hindu》的注册用户并已登录，可以继续参与文章互动。如果你没有账户，请注册并登录后发表评论。用户登录自己的账户后，可以在Vuukle上查看以前的评论"
