   "_dt": 1792679523.0,
   "ageDays": 1.52,
   "summary": "WASHINGTON — The Pentagon and Lockheed Martin announced Thursday a 10-year agreement for the production of 850 F-35 warplanes, underscoring Washington's long-term commitment to the stealth aircraft. The \"framework agreement,\" which the Pentagon said would \"modernize and expand\" the F-35 Lightning II Joint Strike Fighter program, still requires congressional approval and funding.",
   "summary_zh": "华盛顿——五角大楼和洛克希德·马丁公司周四宣布达成一项为期10年的协议，将生产850架F-35战机，凸显华盛顿对这款隐形战机的长期投入。五角大楼表示，这份“框架协议”将使F-35“雷电 II”联合攻击机项目实现“现代化和扩展”，但仍需国会批准并提供资金。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "WASHINGTON — The Pentagon and Lockheed Martin announced Thursday a 10-year agreement for the production of 850 F-35 warplanes, underscoring Washington's long-term commitment to the stealth aircraft. The \"framework agreement,\" which the Pentagon said would \"modernize and expand\" the F-35 Lightning II Joint Strike Fighter program, still requires congressional approval and funding. The F-35, a joint project between the United States and a number of allies, is one of the world's most advanced military aircraft. There are more than 1,375 F-35s based around the world, according to Lockheed. In exchange for the Pentagon's 10-year commitment, Lockheed Martin will fund $7 billion in projects supporting the F-35s, the Pentagon said. \"We have fundamentally changed how we stabilize the American defense industrial base to produce at speed and scale,\" top Pentagon acquisition official Michael Duffey was quoted as saying in the Pentagon announcement. Lockheed pledged to produce the warplanes at a rate of 156 aircraft per year",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
