   "_dt": 1792678500.0,
   "ageDays": 1.54,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription The Union Ministry of Youth Affairs and Sports has sanctioned ₹1.16 crore for the renovation of the dilapidated Government Youth Hostel near Anna Stadium in Tiruchi. In a recent order, the Union Minister of Youth Affairs sanctioned ₹1.83 crore for upgrade of the youth hostels at Bhiwani (Haryana), Tiruchi, and Bhopal (Madhya Pradesh).",
   "summary_zh": "订阅后即可解锁：联邦青年事务与体育部已批准拨款₹1.16 crore，用于翻修蒂鲁吉 Anna体育场附近年久失修的政府青年旅舍。联邦青年事务部长在近期命令中批准拨款₹1.83 crore，用于升级位于比尼亚尼（哈里亚纳邦）、蒂鲁吉和博帕尔（中央邦）的青年旅舍。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription The Union Ministry of Youth Affairs and Sports has sanctioned ₹1.16 crore for the renovation of the dilapidated Government Youth Hostel near Anna Stadium in Tiruchi. The Youth Hostel, attached to the Mera Yuva Bharat - MY Bharat (formerly Nehru Yuva Kendra) office in Tiruch, was shut during the pandemic and remain closed since 2021. The hostel was established to cater to the needs of students and sportspersons travelling to the city from various districts, now lies abandoned. The 80-bed two-storey building that served both the athletes and students has been neglected for years and is in a dilapidated state due to poor maintenance. Earlier, students who travel to Tiruchi from surrounding places to take part in sports competitions and academic events held at the Bharathidasan University and other colleges in the city, used to stay at the hostel. The Central Public Works Department (CPWD) officials had inspected the structure and based on the inspection a proposal was submitted for renovation at a cost of ₹90.62 lakh. However, the Ministry had asked the officials to prune the estimate to less than ₹20 lakh following which a revised proposal was sent for ₹19.92 lakh. Tiruchi Member of Parliament Durai Vaiko too had inspected the hostel in October 2025 and had raised a question on the issue in Parliament. In a recent order, the Union Minister of Youth Affairs sanctioned ₹1.83 crore for upgrade of the youth hostels at Bhiwani (Haryana), Tiruchi, and Bhopal (Madhya Pradesh). The Tiruchi hostel has been allocated the maximum of ₹1.16 crore under the initiative while ₹36 lakh had been allocated to the hostel in Bhiwani and ₹30.60 lakh for the one at Bhopal. “It is good to note that the Ministry has allocated a substantial sum for the Tiruchi hostel as it required major structural repairs,” said Mr. Durai Vaiko expressing happiness over the allocation of funds. Sources in My Bharat office here confirmed the allocation and said that the renovation work would be taken up by the CPWD soon. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
