   "_dt": 1792596239.0,
   "ageDays": 2.49,
   "summary": "President John Mahama says he will appeal to Russian President Vladimir Putin to agree to a ceasefire when he travels to Russia for the Russia-Africa Summit next week. Speaking at the Financial Times Africa Summit in London, President Mahama said he intended to use the visit to urge the Russian leader to halt hostilities. “Indeed, I'm going to Russia for the Russia-Africa summit and try to convince President Putin to have a ceasefire if I can,” he said.",
   "summary_zh": "总统约翰·马哈马表示，他下周前往俄罗斯参加俄非峰会时，将呼吁俄罗斯总统弗拉基米尔·普京同意停火。马哈马总统在伦敦举行的英国《金融时报》非洲峰会上发表讲话时说，他打算利用这次访问敦促俄罗斯领导人停止敌对行动。他说：“确实，我将前往俄罗斯参加俄非峰会，并试图说服普京总统实现停火，如果我能做到的话。”",
   "summarySource": "index",
   "body": "President John Mahama says he will appeal to Russian President Vladimir Putin to agree to a ceasefire when he travels to Russia for the Russia-Africa Summit next week. Speaking at the Financial Times Africa Summit in London, President Mahama said he intended to use the visit to urge the Russian leader to halt hostilities. “Indeed, I'm going to Russia for the Russia-Africa summit and try to convince President Putin to have a ceasefire if I can,” he said. The President also defended Ghana’s investment partnerships with countries across the world, dismissing suggestions that competition among global powers should dictate where the country seeks investment",
