   "title": "Defence Ministry signs ₹770-crore contract with BEL for low-level radars",
   "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/defence-ministry-signs-770-crore-contract-with-bel-for-low-level-radars/article71607636.ece",
   "domain": "thehindu.com",
   "source": "thehindu.com",
   "published": "Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:58:21 +0530",
   "_dt": 1792592901.0,
   "ageDays": 2.53,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription The Ministry of Defence on Wednesday (October 21, 2026) signed a contract worth approximately ₹770 crore with Bharat Electronics Limited (BEL) for the procurement of Improved Low Level Light Weight Radar (LLLR-I), to strengthen the Army’s air defence capabilities against aerial threats, including drones. According to the Ministry, the contract was signed in New Delhi on October 21 in the presence of Defence Secretary Rajesh Kumar Singh.",
   "summary_zh": "国防部于周三（2026年10月21日）与巴拉特电子有限公司（BEL）签署一份价值约770亿卢比的合同，用于采购改进型低空轻型雷达（LLLR-I），以加强陆军对包括无人机在内的空中威胁的防空能力。据国防部称，该合同于10月21日在新德里签署，国防秘书拉杰什·库马尔·辛格出席了签字仪式。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription The Ministry of Defence on Wednesday (October 21, 2026) signed a contract worth approximately ₹770 crore with Bharat Electronics Limited (BEL) for the procurement of Improved Low Level Light Weight Radar (LLLR-I), to strengthen the Army’s air defence capabilities against aerial threats, including drones. According to the Ministry, the contract was signed in New Delhi on October 21 in the presence of Defence Secretary Rajesh Kumar Singh. The LLLR-I system can detect and track fighter-sized targets as well as mini and micro drones. It can also prioritise aerial targets, enabling the Army to respond more effectively to the growing threat posed by unmanned aerial systems (UAS), the Ministry said. The procurement is part of the government’s push to indigenise air defence platforms and strengthen domestic defence manufacturing. It is also expected to support the wider defence industrial ecosystem, including micro, small and medium enterprises (MSMEs). The Ministry said the procurement aligned with the government’s vision of Viksit Bharat @2047 and would contribute to building a resilient, self-reliant and globally competitive defence industry. armed Forces / defence equipment / defence / defence contract Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
