   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription Several farmers owing allegiance to the Left parties resorted to road roko agitations in Tiruchi and other districts in the central region on Wednesday demanding full waiver of crop loans as promised by the Tamilaga Vettri Kazhagam in the run up to the State Assembly elections. The protesting farmers urged the State government to release 9,000 cusecs of Cauvery water to protect the samba paddy crop besides demanding relief for the families who had lost their livelihood.",
   "summary_zh": "多名效忠左翼政党的农民于周三在蒂鲁吉里以及中部地区其他县市采取堵路抗议行动，要求全面免除农贷，正如泰米尔纳德邦胜利联盟在邦议会选举前所承诺的那样。抗议农民敦促邦政府释放9000立方英尺的卡韦里河水以保护桑巴水稻作物，同时要求为失去生计的家庭提供救济。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Several farmers owing allegiance to the Left parties resorted to road roko agitations in Tiruchi and other districts in the central region on Wednesday demanding full waiver of crop loans as promised by the Tamilaga Vettri Kazhagam in the run up to the State Assembly elections. The protesting farmers urged the State government to release 9,000 cusecs of Cauvery water to protect the samba paddy crop besides demanding relief for the families who had lost their livelihood. The road roko agitation in Tiruchi district were held at Tiruverumbur, Lalgudi, and Manapparai leading to the arrest of 170 persons. In neighbouring Pudukottai district, 119 farmers were arrested after they staged road roko agitations at Pudukottai, Gandharvakottai and Alangudi. In Thanjavur district, the road roko stirs were held at 17 places, including Thanjavur, Pattukottai, Peravurani, Kumbakonam, and Ayyampettai. Over 500 persons were arrested. Over 250 farmers were arrested at 10 places in Mayiladuthurai district, including Sirkali, Sembanarkoil, and Kuthalam. Road roko agitations were held in Perambalur, Nagapattinam, and Ariyalur districts, said police sources. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
