   "title": "Diplomacy is necessary, but national security demands transparency and accountability.",
   "url": "https://x.com/findkitty7/status/2113760144438047141",
   "snippet": "Diplomacy is necessary, but national security demands transparency and accountability.\n\nReports of Chinese troops pitching tents near Maja in Arunachal Pradesh, reportedly 6–7 km inside India’s perception of the LAC, raise serious questions. The ITBP chief has also acknowledged ongoing face-offs along the border.\n\nBut why must citizens be cautious about questioning the government on national security?\n\nHow can we speak the truth directly when fear of being labelled anti-national discourages honest questions?\n\nQuestioning the government is not betraying the nation. Demanding answers is not weakening the armed forces.\n\n🇮🇳 India is bigger than any government. National security is bigger than party politics.\n\nWe need facts, transparency and accountability not blind loyalty or silence.",
