   "snippet": "U.S. Ambassador to South Korea Michelle Steel said Wednesday the Korea-U.S. alliance is going through \"turbulence.\" She called it part of a move toward a stronger, more equal partnership.\n\nSpeaking at an AMCHAM event in Seoul, Steel urged South Korea to \"stand up and lead together with the United States\" in the Indo-Pacific. She called China \"the greatest threat in the Indo-Pacific region.\"\n\nShe also said U.S. companies in Korea \"deserve to compete on a level playing field,\" citing searches, audits and fines against American firms. She did not name any company.\n\nIs Seoul ready to take on a bigger leadership role in the alliance?\n\nSource: Yonhap, SBS",
