   "platform": "x",
   "title": "\"Notwithstanding our one China policy.\" That's Felipe Carino III, Manila's deputy chief of mission in Washington, explaining why the Philipp",
   "url": "https://x.com/angeloinchina/status/2113084672972632269",
   "snippet": "\"Notwithstanding our one China policy.\"\n\nThat's Felipe Carino III, Manila's deputy chief of mission in Washington, explaining why the Philippines is \"exploring deeper cooperation with our friends in Taiwan\" on undersea cables.\n\nWhere did he say it ? Not in Manila. At the Center for a New American Security, in Washington. Taiwan's deputy representative spoke at the same seminar.\n\nOn the table: knowledge sharing, capacity building, \"addressing the grey-zone issues\".\nJoint patrols ? He had no details, but said some of it \"may be actually coming to fruition.\"\n\nThe focus is the Bashi Channel, the strip of sea between Luzon and Taiwan.\nThis month the Philippine coast guard already sent its largest ship and a plane to shadow a Chinese research vessel off Batanes.\n\nOne China policy on paper. Taipei as partner in practice. Announced at a US think tank.\n\nSame playbook, new chapter.",
   "body": "\"Notwithstanding our one China policy.\"\n\nThat's Felipe Carino III, Manila's deputy chief of mission in Washington, explaining why the Philippines is \"exploring deeper cooperation with our friends in Taiwan\" on undersea cables.\n\nWhere did he say it ? Not in Manila. At the Center for a New American Security, in Washington. Taiwan's deputy representative spoke at the same seminar.\n\nOn the table: knowledge sharing, capacity building, \"addressing the grey-zone issues\".\nJoint patrols ? He had no details, but said some of it \"may be actually coming to fruition.\"\n\nThe focus is the Bashi Channel, the strip of sea between Luzon and Taiwan.\nThis month the Philippine coast guard already sent its largest ship and a plane to shadow a Chinese research vessel off Batanes.\n\nOne China policy on paper. Taipei as partner in practice. Announced at a US think tank.\n\nSame playbook, new chapter.",
