   "title": "11 African countries on the US highest travel warning list (October 2026)",
   "url": "https://x.com/stats_wire/status/2112880154993111472",
   "snippet": "11 African countries on the US highest travel warning list (October 2026)\n\n1. 🇧🇫 Burkina Faso\n2. 🇨🇫 Central African Republic\n3. 🇹🇩 Chad\n4. 🇨🇩 DR Congo\n5. 🇱🇾 Libya\n6. 🇲🇱 Mali\n7. 🇳🇪 Niger\n8. 🇸🇴 Somalia\n9. 🇸🇸 South Sudan\n10. 🇸🇩 Sudan\n11. 🇺🇬 Uganda\n\nAll 11 carry Level 4: Do Not Travel advisories, the highest US warning level.\n\nReasons include armed conflict, terrorism, kidnapping, violent crime and health emergencies, depending on the country.\n\nNotably, Uganda was raised from Level 3 to Level 4 in May 2026, with health concerns contributing to the change.\n\nSource: US Department of State, Travel Advisories (October 2026).",
   "body": "11 African countries on the US highest travel warning list (October 2026)\n\n1. 🇧🇫 Burkina Faso\n2. 🇨🇫 Central African Republic\n3. 🇹🇩 Chad\n4. 🇨🇩 DR Congo\n5. 🇱🇾 Libya\n6. 🇲🇱 Mali\n7. 🇳🇪 Niger\n8. 🇸🇴 Somalia\n9. 🇸🇸 South Sudan\n10. 🇸🇩 Sudan\n11. 🇺🇬 Uganda\n\nAll 11 carry Level 4: Do Not Travel advisories, the highest US warning level.\n\nReasons include armed conflict, terrorism, kidnapping, violent crime and health emergencies, depending on the country.\n\nNotably, Uganda was raised from Level 3 to Level 4 in May 2026, with health concerns contributing to the change.\n\nSource: US Department of State, Travel Advisories (October 2026).",
